/* ***SHIPPED AT 2, AND THE THREE VALUES ARE THREE DIFFERENT ANSWERS.***
 *
 *   0   mealybug DMG  2 px / 23-of-24     dmg-acid2  PIXEL-PERFECT
 *   1   mealybug DMG  0 px / 24-of-24     dmg-acid2  DIFFER 158/23040,
 *                                         7 scanlines, 133..139
 *   2   mealybug DMG  0 px / 24-of-24     dmg-acid2  PIXEL-PERFECT
 *
 * ***THE COMMENT THAT STOOD HERE SAID "SHIPPED AT 0" AND THE DEFINE BELOW IT
 * SAID 2.***  It was written for the maintainer's 2026-09-06 ruling, which chose 0 when
 * only 0 and 1 existed, and it was not updated when 2 landed at 9eec934.  A
 * block that states the opposite of the line beneath it is worse than no block,
 * and this one stood for a whole cycle.  Left corrected rather than deleted,
 * because the ruling and the reason are the record.
 *
 * THE MAINTAINER'S RULING, VERBATIM, AND IT IS WHY 1 IS NOT SHIPPED: "dmg-acid2 is a
 * rendering test that behaves like real software; it was pixel-perfect and the
 * 24/24 arm visibly breaks it across 7 scanlines.  That is the definition of
 * overfitting to the suite -- the microscope says perfect while the picture gets
 * worse."  ***THE SUITE IS THE INSTRUMENT; GAMES ARE THE GOAL.***
 *
 * AND THE RULING'S OWN CLAUSE IS WHAT LET 2 LAND: "the sandbox keeps hunting an
 * arm that satisfies both authorities; if one is found, the last cell lands
 * later."  One was found.  A choice made to protect an authority is not a
 * ceiling on the mechanism, and this is the case that shows the difference.
 *
 * ***HOW 2 WAS FOUND -- BY CENSUS, AND IT EXISTS NOWHERE ELSE IN THIS TREE.***
 * The insertion fires on lines where the window comparison happens.  Counting
 * its firings with the enable-seen flag beside them:
 *
 *     dmg-acid2                    150 firings, EVERY ONE WITH seen = 0
 *     the two mealybug rows that    both fire with seen = 1
 *     need the insertion
 *
 * LCDC.5 was never set during mode 3 on any of acid2's lines, so the window
 * comparison is not being made on them at all.  ***A COMPARISON AGAINST WX
 * CANNOT LEAVE AN ARTEFACT ON A LINE WHERE THE COMPARISON IS NOT BEING MADE***
 * -- so gating the insertion on gb->win_en_seen removes exactly acid2's 150 and
 * keeps exactly mealybug's two.  The gate is at src/gb.c around line 8300.
 *
 * WHY IT WAS INVISIBLE FOR A CYCLE: this arm was developed against the mealybug
 * board, and dmg-acid2 lives in our net test and not on that board.  The 2-px
 * gain and the 158-px regression were the SAME EDIT, and only a whole-net run
 * separates them.  Six other window arms were cleared one at a time and all
 * leave acid2 broken; this one alone restores it. */
#ifndef WIN_INSERT_ZERO
#define WIN_INSERT_ZERO 2
#endif
