#endif
/* RUN_IRQ_LOOK_DMG -- THE RUNNING PROCESSOR SEES A PPU REQUEST TWO DOTS EARLIER
 * THAN THE HALTED ONE (2026-10-28).
 * Three hardware tables, each verified by its author, disagree with one
 * sampling point:
 *   AGE stat-int-dmgC (a RUNNING processor, NOPs, takes the mode-0, mode-2 and
 *     mode-1 STAT interrupts): the mode-0 dispatch lands in the same machine
 *     cycle for SCX 0-2, the next for 3-6, the next for 7; ours grouped 0 | 1-4 |
 *     5-8, i.e. our request was 2 dots late for this processor; its mode-2 and
 *     mode-1 rows want the dispatch one machine cycle earlier too.
 *   AGE halt-m0-interrupt-dmgC (HALT with IME clear: the halt bug repeats the
 *     next byte when the request is already up AS THE HALT EXECUTES): SCX 0-2
 *     already up, 3-7 not -- the same 2 dots.
 *   Mooneye hblank_ly_scx_timing-GS (EI; HALT, a HALTED processor woken by the
 *     same mode-0 request): groups 0 | 1-4 | 5-7, the timing we had.
 * So the request is where it was for the halted processor, and the running
 * processor's sample (the instruction-boundary test and HALT's own test) sees
 * two dots further on.  Measured, not taken from any source: an earlier refused
 * arm M0_IRQ_LEAD_DMG 2 moved the request for both and broke the Mooneye row.
 * SCOPE: THE END-OF-DRAWING (MODE-0) REQUEST ONLY (RUN_IRQ_LOOK_EDGES 2).  The
 * same look at the line start (mode 2, LYC, vertical blank; RUN_IRQ_LOOK_EDGES
 * 1|2) also passes stat-int's mode-2 and (with VB_MODE_DOT 6) mode-1 rows, but it
 * moves every mode-2-interrupt-timed write one machine cycle earlier: mealybug
 * 24/24 -> 2/24 and AGE m3-bg-lcdc (DMG) fails.  Our write leads were fitted
 * with today's line-start dispatch, so that half was DECLINED until they
 * were re-derived.
 * REDEVELOPED (2026-10-28):
 * RUN_IRQ_LOOK_EDGES 3 together with DMG_WRITE_LAG 4 (the drawing-register
 * writes land one machine cycle later than the leads fitted under the late
 * dispatch put them), LINE0_DISPATCH_LAG 3, VB_MODE_DOT 6 and DMG_HALT_TEST_END 2.
 * mealybug 24/24 at 0 px, AGE stat-int-dmgC passes, stat-mode-window-dmgC 44 -> 6
 * and stat-mode-sprites-dmgC 43 -> 9 wrong cells.
 * HOW: at an instruction boundary of a running DMG near a request edge, the PPU
 * runs RUN_IRQ_LOOK_DMG dots early and the machine cycle owes that many fewer
 * (pend_dots goes negative and ppu_pay carries the remainder, DMG only; on the
 * DMG pend_dots was never negative before).  Gated to the dots where a request
 * can rise (line start, the end of drawing) and off when the next instruction's
 * second machine cycle reads or writes memory, so no access moves.
 * LABEL: MECHANISM for the split (two sampling points), FITTED for the 2.
 * Off arm: RUN_IRQ_LOOK_DMG 0. */
#ifndef RUN_IRQ_LOOK_EDGES
#define RUN_IRQ_LOOK_EDGES 3
#endif
#ifndef RUN_IRQ_LOOK_DMG
#define RUN_IRQ_LOOK_DMG 2
#endif
/* DMG_WRITE_LAG -- A DRAWING-REGISTER WRITE LANDS ONE MACHINE CYCLE LATER THAN
 * THE OLD LEADS PUT IT (2026-10-28).
 * The old per-register leads (BGP_LEAD 2, OBP_LEAD 3, LCDC_LEAD 2, SCX_WRITE_LEAD
 * 1, SCY_EARLY 1, WX_LEAD 2) placed each write 1-3 dots BEFORE its own machine
 * cycle began.  They were fitted on mealybug, whose every write is timed from a
 * mode-2 interrupt taken by a running processor -- and that dispatch was one
 * machine cycle late (AGE stat-int-dmgC, its author's hardware table).  With
 * the dispatch on time (RUN_IRQ_LOOK_EDGES 3) every mealybug write arrives four
 * dots earlier, and the pictures (21 of 24 photographed on hardware) stay
 * exactly where they were only if each write lands four dots later: the PPU runs
 * DMG_WRITE_LAG dots before the register's own delivery code and the machine
 * cycle owes that many fewer.  Net placement: 1-3 dots INSIDE the write's own
 * machine cycle instead of before it.
 * Measured: mealybug 24/24 at 0 px (2/24 at 52,489 px with the dispatch alone);
 * docboy agreement 26,307 -> 17,299 px (279 -> 376 identical of 572), the whole
 * change_bgp_from_read_stat_hblank_mode family (81 rows: BGP written after a
 * POLLED STAT read, a timing the dispatch does not touch) to 0 px.  Cost on
 * the same instrument: 24 window_turn_off rows 17 -> 20/22 px and
 * change_bgp_from_boot 52 -> 56 (window disable now lands after the takeover;
 * our mid-tile abort is not modelled).
 * SCOPE: LCDC, SCY, SCX, BGP, OBP0, OBP1, WX while the LCD is on, DMG only
 * (DMG_WRITE_LAG_MASK, bit n = $FF40+n).  WY is left out: no table we hold puts a
 * WY write behind a running dispatch, and docboy's
 * window_trigger_wy_blink_during_next_hblank_round1 stops settling with it in.
 * LABEL: MECHANISM (one placement for every drawing register), the 4 is the
 * dispatch shift it compensates.  Off arm: 0. */
#ifndef DMG_WRITE_LAG
#define DMG_WRITE_LAG 4
#endif
