/* STRUCTURAL EXCLUSION, added after the knob audit found this pair shadowed.
 * Both branches gate on sx == 0 and OBJ_X0_OUTPUT is tested FIRST in
 * ppu_object_at, so a non-zero OBJ_X0_OUTPUT makes OBJ_PREVIS_AT0 unreachable.
 * Until today that was a SILENT no-op: the knob accepted a value and reported
 * nothing, which is the class this guard exists to make impossible.
 *
 * Setting both is now a COMPILE ERROR rather than a silently ignored value.
 * Build with OBJ_X0_OUTPUT=0 to reach the previs branch.
 *
 * The lever preserved here is worth -48 px across ten tests when reachable, and
 * it is NOT retired: nothing measured says it is wrong, and retiring it would
 * remove the evidence along with the lever.
 *
 * WARNING ABOUT THAT NUMBER, because it reads the wrong way in a table.
 *
 * RE-DERIVED AT BASE 2896 (after LCDC_PEND 4 -> 5 shipped).  The figures this
 * paragraph carried are RETIRED BY NAME rather than deleted: it read
 * "scores 5388 at 6/24 -- ONE MORE PASS than HEAD (5121, 5/24) and 68 px better
 * than the pre-seam 5456 at the same 6/24".  Those were true against base 5121
 * and stopped being about this core when the board moved.
 *
 * At base 2896 the arm scores 3263 at 6/24: still ONE MORE PASS than HEAD
 * (2896, 5/24), and now 367 px WORSE rather than 68 px better than anything.
 * RE-DERIVED AT BASE 1892 (cycle 1 shipped): the arm scores 2229 at 6/24 against
 * HEAD's 1892 at 5/24 -- one more pass, 337 px worse.  The base-2896 figures are
 * retired by name; the argument is unchanged for the third base running.
 * THE ARGUMENT IS UNCHANGED AND IS STRONGER -- the awkward half, an arm that
 * beat a historical base, is gone, and what remains is an arm that buys a pass
 * by being worse.  IT IS NOT A CONFIGURATION TO BE IN.  That arm encodes 10 dots at the
 * seam (OAM X = 8), and all three authorities at that cell -- the mealybug
 * author's law, SameBoy and docboy -- say 11, which is what HEAD produces.
 * So the arm with more passes is the arm that disagrees with everything we hold
 * at the cell in question.  Passes and mechanism point opposite ways here, and
 * the mechanism has already been ruled to win once on this same axis.
 * It is a lever for INVESTIGATING the seam, not a candidate for shipping. */
#if OBJ_X0_OUTPUT && OBJ_PREVIS_AT0
#error "OBJ_PREVIS_AT0 is unreachable while OBJ_X0_OUTPUT is set: both gate sx == 0 and OBJ_X0_OUTPUT wins. Build with OBJ_X0_OUTPUT=0 to use it."
#endif
/* THE READY POINT AS ITS OWN STATE, decoupled from the fetcher's phase.
 *
 * obj_win_open() defines the on-screen ready point AS a phase of the fetch cycle,
 * so it IS the push comb and cannot be displaced from it: measured, a WX = 7
 * takeover moves both by exactly +5. Lab A measured the oracle's two moving in
 * OPPOSITE directions, push -2 and ready +6, so a structure in which they are one
 * quantity cannot express what has been measured.
 *
 * This reads the same three-of-eight window off an ABSOLUTE comb instead.
 * OBJ_READY_PHASE is a NAMED CONSTANT, not a derived quantity: it is chosen so
 * that on a bare line the window falls exactly where the fetch phase puts it
 * today, which makes every bare-line instrument unchanged BY CONSTRUCTION rather
 * than by luck. On a takeover line the comb no longer follows the fetcher, and
 * that difference is the whole measurement.
 *
 * The origin is a constant and is named as one. Nobody derives it -- not us, not
 * either oracle -- and it is not fitted to make any cell land. */
#ifndef OBJ_READY_STATE
#define OBJ_READY_STATE 0
#endif
/* ARM/DISARM. An object stall DISARMS the ready window; the next background push
 * RE-ARMS it. A disarmed object is served at once (notice + 6); an armed one
 * waits for the window as before. The flag starts ARMED at mode-3 entry, so the
 * line's first object is unaffected.
 *
 * This is a RESTORATION, not an addition: measured before it was written, this
 * core already produces the rule's answer at every cell that does not hang --
 * 6, 6, 11, 10, 9, 7, 11 at separations 1, 2, 8, 9, 10, 12, 16, seven of seven.
 * What was missing is the branch at separations where the window is closed, where
 * we produced nothing at all.
 *
 * THE SCAR, and it is why the guarantee below is now stated in terms of arming.
 * The comment on the wait's threshold said: "It cannot deadlock: reaching this
 * threshold needs only the fetcher to advance, never an empty FIFO." That is
 * right about what it checked -- the condition is not the push's own precondition
 * -- and wrong about what it assumed. The fetcher DOES advance during the wait
 * (ppu_fetcher_step is called on the wait dot), but it advances to step 4 and
 * PARKS there, because the push at step 4 requires an empty BG FIFO, and the FIFO
 * cannot drain while the wait holds lx still. So reaching the threshold needs the
 * fetcher to advance PAST the push, and that needs exactly the empty FIFO the
 * comment said it did not need. The wait did await its own completion, one level
 * removed. Nothing in the text was checkable against that, because the assumption
 * was never stated.
 *
 * Arming cannot deadlock in the same way: a disarmed object does not wait at all,
 * so it cannot wait on a condition its own waiting prevents. */
#ifdef ARMTRACE
#include <stdio.h>
#define gbtrace(...) fprintf(stderr, __VA_ARGS__)
#endif
#ifdef ARMSCAN
#include <stdio.h>
#define gbscan(...) fprintf(stderr, __VA_ARGS__)
#endif
#ifdef ARMCOVER
#include <stdio.h>
#define gbcov(...) fprintf(stderr, __VA_ARGS__)
#endif
#ifdef SEQTRACE
#include <stdio.h>
static unsigned long gb_seqno;
#define gbseq(...) do { fprintf(stderr, "%06lu ", ++gb_seqno); \
                        fprintf(stderr, __VA_ARGS__); } while (0)
#endif
/* The push is TWO events when the FIFO is non-empty at readiness: the fetcher
 * reaches step 4 with data (READY) and parks until the FIFO drains (COMMIT).
 * Measured five dots apart after an object stall. Arming at READY rather than
 * at COMMIT is Lab B's arm/commit split, confirmed on this core with their
 * monotonic-sequence method. */
/* PARKED: the fetcher holds data at its push step and cannot commit because the
 * FIFO is not empty. A waiting object freezes lx, the FIFO drains only as lx
 * advances, so a parked fetcher plus a waiting object can never resolve itself.
 * The window is shut in that state (parked is pos 7), so the wait would be
 * forever. Serving is the only exit, which makes the window open by definition
 * whenever the fetcher is parked.
 *
 * THE SCAR: the original no-deadlock comment reasoned about the condition it had
 * written and never about whether the state machine could reach it. Reachability
 * is not a side question here -- it IS the rule.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * SHIPPED AT 1, 2026-08-29.  THIS IS THE FIX FOR THE ZELDA/SUPER MARIO LAND
 * FREEZE, AND IT WAS ALREADY IN THE TREE.
 *
 * THE SHIP THAT CAUSED THE REGRESSION, NAMED AND NOT SOFTENED (the maintainer's
 * instruction): d05637d, 2026-08-19 17:22, "Ship the object model per the maintainer's
 * ruling: 12418 -> 8890" -- the phase-keyed object wait that replaced the
 * per-alignment stall.  The commit before it produced 0 short lines and it
 * produced 146.  It bought 3528 px on 24 synthetic stimuli and deadlocked a
 * rendering path no cell exercises.  This is its SECOND cost; unlike the first
 * it was invisible to every gate we own until a real cartridge was looked at.
 *
 * AND THE FIX HAS BEEN SITTING HERE, DEFAULTED OFF, SINCE THAT SAME SHIP.  All
 * four arming knobs were committed, gate-passed and reachable by NO COMMITTED
 * BUILD -- the orphaned-instrument shape, in a fix rather than in an
 * instrument.  our recorded test --flags finds orphaned emitters; nothing in
 * this tree looks for an orphaned REMEDY.
 *
 * WHY THIS KNOB AND NOT THE ONE NAMED AFTER THE MECHANISM.  OBJ_ARM_DISARM
 * zeroes the freeze on all seven titles too -- and MOVES k = 8, a NON-HANGING
 * cell, from 11 to 6.  our work list says in terms that a fix which unhangs
 * while changing any non-hanging cost has ADDED a mechanism rather than
 * restored one.  That is a rejection, not a trade to be priced, and it fires on
 * the knob whose name matches the mechanism.  OBJ_PARK_OPEN leaves all seven
 * non-hanging cells EXACTLY unchanged and produces a value at all five hanging
 * ones.  The other three knobs stay 0 and are not part of this ship.
 *
 * WHAT THE BOARD SAYS ABOUT THIS: NOTHING, AND THAT IS RECORDED AS A VACUITY
 * RATHER THAN LEFT TO READ AS SUPPORT.  All five candidates produce
 * BIT-IDENTICAL boards.  No mealybug cell contains two objects at k = 3..7 --
 * which is exactly why this defect reached a shipped title unseen.  The board
 * is evidence that the fence HOLDS and is no evidence whatever FOR this
 * candidate.  The discriminator was the k-table and the two cartridges.
 * =========================================================================== */
#ifndef OBJ_PARK_OPEN
#define OBJ_PARK_OPEN 1
#endif
#ifndef OBJ_ARM_AT_READY
#define OBJ_ARM_AT_READY 0
#endif
#ifndef OBJ_ARM_DISARM
#define OBJ_ARM_DISARM 0
#endif
